# Acceptance scenarios

When adding or editing a page scenario:

- Add a `Scenario` to `SCENARIOS` in `tests/acceptance/cases.py`.
- Each item in `operations` is one tool call, in list order. The class-to-tool table is the module docstring of `tests/acceptance/operations.py`. Use those classes.
- The driver owns the page id. Leave ids out of the scenario.
- `blocks` is semantic HTML, checked with `assert_semantic`. Record what a reader sees. Leave out stylesheets, classes, wrappers, and the page shell.

```python
Scenario(
    name="publish-a-page",
    title="Team handbook",
    operations=(Publish(title="Team handbook", content="## Welcome\n"),),
    blocks=({"h2": "Welcome"},),
)
```
